[{:db/id 17592186087774 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5e9b8a76-fadd-5c5e-88d1-453c1509beac" "question-5dbc9673-510f-532c-a004-54ed22aabfa7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5e9b8a76-fadd-5c5e-88d1-453c1509beac" :question/id #uuid "5e9b8a76-fadd-5c5e-88d1-453c1509beac" :question/math-academy-id "q-64795" :question/problem "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-18{y}^{′}+81y=0$ for $y=y(t),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-18\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}+81{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-18\\lambda +81) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-18\\lambda +81 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -9)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =9$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{9t}$ and $t{e}^{9t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $3{e}^{-9t}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-585f5d02-4d6c-51a6-9fd9-0f3602ee74e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-585f5d02-4d6c-51a6-9fd9-0f3602ee74e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "585f5d02-4d6c-51a6-9fd9-0f3602ee74e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c8f68714-c0ba-58d7-8203-728b2921b006" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e69ea800-ad27-5d19-8fda-f9c165e154aa" "answer-c635f663-c965-5072-9ef5-15319fccaa59" "answer-c8f68714-c0ba-58d7-8203-728b2921b006" "answer-05281020-031d-5d2a-808e-01688d4b6930" "answer-9983f332-f05f-500a-8acb-70984c9621d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e69ea800-ad27-5d19-8fda-f9c165e154aa" :answer/id #uuid "e69ea800-ad27-5d19-8fda-f9c165e154aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7t{e}^{9t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c635f663-c965-5072-9ef5-15319fccaa59" :answer/id #uuid "c635f663-c965-5072-9ef5-15319fccaa59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{9t}+5t{e}^{9t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f68714-c0ba-58d7-8203-728b2921b006" :answer/id #uuid "c8f68714-c0ba-58d7-8203-728b2921b006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-9t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05281020-031d-5d2a-808e-01688d4b6930" :answer/id #uuid "05281020-031d-5d2a-808e-01688d4b6930" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{9t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9983f332-f05f-500a-8acb-70984c9621d3" :answer/id #uuid "9983f332-f05f-500a-8acb-70984c9621d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{9t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5dbc9673-510f-532c-a004-54ed22aabfa7" :question/id #uuid "5dbc9673-510f-532c-a004-54ed22aabfa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-64796" :question/problem "Given the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{16}y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{1}{16}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\lambda +\\frac{1}{16} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda +\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x/4}$ and $x{e}^{-x/4}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $2{e}^{-4x}+3x{e}^{-x/4}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-47117b4f-de1f-5179-8ffa-cfd17b335562"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47117b4f-de1f-5179-8ffa-cfd17b335562" :answer-field/id #uuid "47117b4f-de1f-5179-8ffa-cfd17b335562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c7c927a-01c3-5ee9-9a6b-b90fcf3476e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c7c927a-01c3-5ee9-9a6b-b90fcf3476e6" "answer-1c7e410e-ff0e-513f-b439-59db85b21e9e" "answer-19665675-933f-562b-92c2-453f3aa6a7c3" "answer-59ac1266-2808-5904-a986-8f81e5f69ca0" "answer-3bc60826-5099-595c-bb90-6813ebbf7d31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c7c927a-01c3-5ee9-9a6b-b90fcf3476e6" :answer/id #uuid "6c7c927a-01c3-5ee9-9a6b-b90fcf3476e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-4x}+3x{e}^{-x/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c7e410e-ff0e-513f-b439-59db85b21e9e" :answer/id #uuid "1c7e410e-ff0e-513f-b439-59db85b21e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-x/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19665675-933f-562b-92c2-453f3aa6a7c3" :answer/id #uuid "19665675-933f-562b-92c2-453f3aa6a7c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x{e}^{-x/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59ac1266-2808-5904-a986-8f81e5f69ca0" :answer/id #uuid "59ac1266-2808-5904-a986-8f81e5f69ca0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{-x/4}-x{e}